course: dictionary
lesson: 13981
title: Words for moving
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Locomotion is a noun. It means the ability to move from one place to another, or the way an animal or person moves. «Kangaroos use hopping as their main locomotion.» Here locomotion tells you how the kangaroo travels, which is by hopping.
explain: Animals use their bodies for locomotion. Muscles and bones let you walk and run. Fish use fins to swim, and birds use wings to fly. «Snakes have no legs, so they use slithering for locomotion.» Each animal has its own way of moving.
explain: Locomotion is also a word from history. Steam locomotion changed how people travelled. A locomotive is a train engine, and it is a related word. Locomotion No. 1 was one of the first steam railway engines, built in 1825.
fact: Locomotion means the ability to move from one place to another.
fact: Animal locomotion includes walking, running, hopping, slithering, swimming and flying.
fact: Muscles, bones, fins and wings all help a body move.
fact: A locomotive is a train engine, a related word to locomotion.
fact: Locomotion No. 1 was one of the first steam railway engines, built in 1825.
exercise: «Snakes have no legs, so they use slithering as their locomotion.» What does locomotion mean here? | A snake's favourite food | The sound a snake makes | The place where a snake sleeps | *The way something moves
exercise: Which body part helps a bird with its locomotion when it flies? | *Wings | Fins | Ears
exercise: What is a locomotive? | A type of bird | *A train engine | A kind of rock | A sports game
test: Which of these is NOT a type of animal locomotion? | Flying | *Sleeping | Hopping | Swimming
test: Locomotion No. 1 was one of the first steam railway engines. In which year was it built? | 1925 | *1825 | 1852 | 1625
exam: «The frog uses hopping as its locomotion.» Which body parts help the frog hop? | *Muscles and bones | Fins only | Feathers only | Hair
